---
title: "gpg_encrypt (Daily DB Backup Workflow)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_read_pass: GPG_PASSPHRASE = secrets.GPG_PASSPHRASE
    q_read_pass --> q_validate: GPG_PASSPHRASE is set
    q_read_pass --> q_error: GPG_PASSPHRASE is empty
    q_validate --> q_encrypt: echo GPG_PASSPHRASE | gpg --batch --yes --passphrase-fd 0 --symmetric --cipher-algo AES256 -o backup.dump.gpg backup.dump
    q_encrypt --> q_check: encryption completes
    q_check --> q_delete_plain: backup.dump.gpg exists
    q_check --> q_error: encryption failed
    q_delete_plain --> [*]: rm backup.dump
    q_error --> [*]: step fails

    note right of q_encrypt
        INV-001: AES256 symmetric cipher used for encryption
        INV-002: passphrase passed via fd 0 (stdin), not command-line argument
        INV-003: --batch --yes suppresses interactive prompts
    end note

    note right of q_delete_plain
        INV-004: plaintext backup.dump MUST be deleted immediately after successful encryption
        INV-005: only backup.dump.gpg remains after this step
    end note
